  "id": "Compound::DB08896 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Regorafenib is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a complex network of interactions involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Regorafenib, as a member of the Cytochrome P450 2c9 inhibitors class, may influence Cyp2c19 through indirect mechanisms. Specifically, Regorafenib is linked to Fluconazole and Zafirlukast, both of which bind to Cyp2c19, indicating a potential role in modulating Cyp2c19 activity. The lowest common ancestor of these interactions points to the broader class of organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds, suggesting a possible pathway where Regorafenib indirectly affects Cyp2c19 by influencing the activity of other compounds that bind to it. This integrated evidence highlights a mechanism where Regorafenib may exert its effects on Cyp2c19 through the modulation of other drugs that share a common chemical structure, thereby influencing Cyp2c19's function in metabolic processes.",
